ble Weiser margin, reinforced by Republican crossover endorsements and a GOP nominee running outside the party establishment. The main caution is that this is an open seat with no statewide polling, so uncertainty stays somewhat wider than usual.", "watch": "Any late statewide polling showing Marx within single digits, or a decisive shift in the national environment toward Republicans in the campaign's final weeks, would narrow this forecast.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Jared Polis (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Colorado's governorship is open as Jared Polis steps aside due to term limits, and Democrats hold a clear edge in a state that has favored their candidates by roughly six points. Attorney General Phil Weiser enters the general election with broad name recognition and a unified expert consensus behind him: six of seven major raters place the race in the Solid or Safe Democratic column, with the seventh calling it Likely Democratic. Betting markets on all major platforms price a Democratic win at 97 percent.\n\nRepublican Victor Marx runs as a political outsider who has dismissed the need for party establishment approval, and his campaign has publicized favorable polling only from the state's reddest county. Former Republican Congressman Ken Buck's endorsement of Weiser, alongside other GOP figures, underscores the Democrat's cross-party appeal. With no statewide public polling available, the picture rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets, all pointing the same direction.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9695, "margin": 12.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9628, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9677, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9635, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9625, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "